@Notes for developers: use `getlistingstatus` to check one list by ID
@Note by script wrriters: Use `Setlistingstatus` to modify the condition of a list in this script
Use: This script reveals information on a list when you double-click it. It also has a functionality that updates a property property by modifying this property in the graphical interface, or by modifying the value of a variable in a text block.
Right -click on any list input. Choose "Listing Detail" from the menu that appears. The menu will develop and include a list area full of list details. You can then extend these items as much as you want to see detailed information. When you start to double-click on something to get more information, you will want a "divided window". Do it at the top left, just above the program icon. In this way, you can see all the things open in a single screen without having to return to different windows, which is tedious.
